@@ -0,0 +1,316 @@
+# FoldGPT auxiliary engine: local runtime boundary
+
+Base: `rust-v0.153.4`, commit `3d2ee51ca2d5db578f328aa75e20aa22c0197c9a`.
+
+This checkout is a separate engine. It does not alter the official application's
+files or its bundled engine. Nothing in this increment selects this engine on a
+phone or starts an Android worker.
+
+## Implemented boundary
+
+Application bootstrap may supply an authenticated `Arc<dyn LocalRuntime>` to
+`PreparedEnvironmentManager::build_with_local_runtime`. This uses the discovered
+environment configuration, registers the provider as the real `local` environment,
+and keeps `Environment::is_remote()` false. The default, local lookup and registry
+lookup share one `Environment` instance. A configuration excluding local
+execution, including a Noise-only configuration, is rejected.
+
+The effective app-server startup now accepts the trusted Rust bootstrap value
+returned by `AppServerRuntimeOptions::with_local_runtime`. It discovers the
+configured environments and calls `build_with_local_runtime` before exposing the
+server transport. Ordinary options preserve the default construction path. A
+registration error aborts startup; no client request or serialized config field
+can supply this runtime. User-config suppression retains its existing environment
+discovery behavior. Application-owned configuration is still loaded on the
+controller before this boundary. Provider registration does not admit
+`ExecutorOnly` paths.
+
+The subsequent configuration-layer entry point
+`load_config_layers_state_with_project_fs` keeps packaged/system/user/managed
+sources on their controller filesystem and supplies the project's actual
+filesystem for discovery, trust canonicalization, TOML and inherited project
+hooks. Project layers retain their normal authority, precedence and disabled
+state. Non-missing provider failures abort loading, and typed project diagnostics
+locate errors in the captured provider text, preserving the actual project path.
+App-server `config/read` with a cwd selects this entry point when its real local
+environment has an injected runtime. Calls without a cwd retain controller
+configuration loading. The existing unified loader preserves legacy behavior.
+The injected public read also resolves feature flags from this same loaded
+stack, including managed constraints and process runtime overrides. Its feature
+reporting no longer launches a second controller `ConfigBuilder` load.
+
+This stage does not yet wire `ConfigBuilder` or referenced instructions/agent-role
+files through separate providers. AGENTS delivery is unchanged. It does not grant
+policy: the selected filesystem may reject these trusted configuration reads.
+The native factory still requires a separate bootstrap-owned read authority;
+`sandbox: None` is not made universally admissible. `ExecutorOnly` remains refused.
+The separate CLI/TUI error renderer still reads source excerpts from the host;
+this renderer is not part of the public app-server `config/read` path.
+
+The provider owns `ExecBackend`, `ExecutorFileSystem`, metadata and readiness.
+Process sandbox ownership, filesystem sandbox ownership and direct controller
+path access are separate declarations. Ordinary local and remote environments
+retain their previous behavior.
+
+This increment admits only `ControllerPathAccess::Shared`. An `ExecutorOnly`
+provider is rejected at registration, before the unadapted direct controller
+routes can execute. The declaration is already explicit so those routes can be
+adapted without conflating sandbox ownership with path visibility.
+
+The model's unified execution route now chooses the sandbox owner independently
+of host locality and sends the existing typed `ExecParams`, including sandbox and
+network context, to the selected backend. Apply-patch does the same for filesystem
+sandbox context. Existing approval and permission resolution remain in the
+controller. There is no backend retry through an unsandboxed controller launcher.
+An implementation must reject unsupported policy semantics before mutation.
+
+The turn now obtains an injected local runtime's shell, home, temporary roots,
+platform OS and snapshot capability from `Environment::info()`, even when its
+paths are shared. Missing optional metadata stays missing. An info error or an
+unrecognized runtime shell fails environment resolution instead of selecting
+the controller shell. Model commands use that runtime's direct shell mode and
+reported executable, including when the model names that exact installed path;
+other shell types remain explicitly unsupported until runtime discovery exists.
+The controller's V1 snapshot launcher does not execute an injected runtime shell.
+Executor snapshots still require the actual advertised V2 implementation; this
+increment does not implement snapshots in Bionic or activate ExecutorOnly paths.
+Reported Android uses POSIX command-classification semantics, alongside Linux
+and macOS; unknown platforms retain the existing conservative treatment.
+
+The independent `OwnedProcessDriver` adapter accepts bounded split output streams,
+queued stdin, real exit notifications and fallible native controls. Its producer
+must retain descendant ownership and apply backpressure. A successful control
+request is not proof of cleanup; the runtime must attest cleanup separately. This
+adapter is not yet selected by the unified execution injection route, which uses
+the existing `ExecProcess` API.
+
+`ExecProcessEventReceiver::from_owned_receiver` now admits a bounded, exclusively
+owned event stream from a runtime outside the exec-server crate. This removes the
+mandatory broadcast hop at that public boundary. The producer must apply
+backpressure and retain control independently of event consumption. A dropped
+transport does not become a fabricated successful exit; `Exited`, `Closed` and
+`Failed` remain distinct. This is available to an actual native `ExecProcess`
+implementation, which still must supply its retained reads and native controls.
+
+`ExecServerLocalRuntime::connect` now supplies a production wire adapter over one
+already-authenticated, bootstrap-owned pair of asynchronous I/O streams. It
+reuses the official ExecServer client and typed process/filesystem implementations,
+without a remote Environment, executable, URL or replacement transport. The
+bootstrap owns authentication and the independent native cleanup channel. The
+adapter never attaches the official stdio child supervisor, whose process-tree
+kill policy would conflict with that ownership.
+
+This fixed transport has no reconnect strategy. Process start is not replayed
+after sending; disconnect closes RPC admission even for previously cloned
+backends. A lost native read returns an error instead of the resumable client's
+synthetic `exited/closed` failure response; process events report `Failed` without
+inventing an exit. `disconnect()` closes transport only, and never attests native
+cleanup. The filesystem adapter retains the complete typed sandbox context,
+including cwd even when the ordinary remote helper could omit it.
+
+The official wire client retains its existing bounded broadcast/replay buffers;
+it does not automatically use `from_owned_receiver`. The new real integration
+test uses the native factory's explicit 32 KiB output cap. It does not establish
+lossless arbitrary-size output for this adapter.
+
+## Integration still required
+
+The following are explicit limits of this increment, not supported Android paths:
+
+- Authenticate, start and monitor the native service in the real application
+  bootstrap, then supply it to the Rust entry point. No deployed application
+  activation path exists.
+- Qualify the native factory behind `ExecServerLocalRuntime` on Android and
+  complete its unsupported request semantics. The same actual factory and C
+  supervisor are connected in the PC test, but this does not prove Android rights.
+- Consume `ControllerPathAccess` in host command, terminal, one-shot shell,
+  plugin-attribution, complete shell discovery/snapshots and local file-watch routes.
+  Several existing local branches still assume controller-visible filesystem
+  paths. Registration currently rejects `ExecutorOnly` until those routes are addressed.
+- Connect lossless owned output to the real process managers, including cancellation,
+  disconnect propagation, descendant cleanup and cleanup quarantine.
+- Implement and qualify the actual Android policy enforcement and lifecycle.
+  These traits make no claim that namespace, Landlock or bubblewrap is available.
+- Build/link the auxiliary engine for its actual GNU ARM64 target and validate its
+  launch within the existing application identity. No Android engine build or
+  complete model/UI execution is demonstrated by PC tests.
+
+## Validation cases
+
+The new local runtime tests cover actual PC child-process execution, exit 23,
+filesystem content, identity consistency, readiness/disconnection delegation,
+configuration conflicts and policy refusals without fallback. The core integration
+test scripts model tool calls through the standard response test harness while
+executing real process/filesystem operations; it checks successful execution and
+apply-patch, followed by required-sandbox refusals before writes.
+
+The owned driver tests use real Python child processes and one-chunk output
+backpressure, preserving 771,006 stdout bytes and 385,500 stderr bytes, stdin EOF,
+exit 23, unsupported controls, termination and reaping. These are PC transport
+tests and do not certify Android process ownership.
+
+Verified on WSL Ubuntu 24.04 with Rust 1.95.0, as the unprivileged
+`foldgpt-build` user:
+
+- `just test -p codex-exec-server -p codex-utils-pty --locked`: 552 tests run,
+  549 passed, three failed, three skipped. All four new runtime tests and both
+  owned-driver tests passed.
+- `just test -p codex-core --test all injected_local_runtime --locked`: the one
+  selected model-dispatch integration test passed; 1,643 tests were filtered out.
+- The three package failures are the existing remote shell-snapshot cases
+  `shell_snapshot_v2_filters_profile_exports_and_stays_in_memory::remote_sandbox`
+  and `shell_snapshot_v2_capture_failure_falls_back_and_retries` for
+  `remote_pipe_recovery` and `remote_tty_recovery`. The identical cases failed on
+  the pristine base commit with only the mechanical lock normalization below
+  (12 of 15 selected baseline cases passed). This increment does not repair those
+  upstream snapshot defects or claim a green complete package suite.
+
+The complete core and workspace test suites were not run. Linux PC verification
+does not establish Windows, ARM64 linking, Android or application UI compatibility.
+
+`just fix` was scoped to the three changed crates and completed. `just fmt`
+completed for all repository formatter groups; its two uv project environments
+were located separately on WSL's Linux filesystem because installing wheel files
+on the Windows mount returned `EPERM`. No formatter implementation was changed.
+`just bazel-lock-update` completed under Bazel 9.0.0 without changing
+`MODULE.bazel.lock`. Its existing dependency-version and crate-annotation warnings
+were retained; no dependencies were upgraded to silence them.
+The final `just clippy` check for the same three crates completed with only the
+pre-existing unused `body_json` import warning in `openai_file_mcp.rs`.
+
+The follow-up `just test -p codex-exec-server --test owned_process_events --locked`
+passed both tests. An external-crate `ExecProcess` fixture launches a real compiled
+child, sends binary stdin and preserves all 1,156,506 stdout/stderr bytes plus the
+actual exit 23 through a one-event queue. Retained reads and transport-failure
+reporting are also exercised. The fixture uses PC pipe control and a fixed 2 MiB
+retention limit for its known output; it is not a production native backend or a
+new application/model qualification.
+The matching `process::tests` library selection also passed all 15 cases,
+including retained replay, late output and process lifecycle regressions.
+
+The real Rust-to-Python/native-factory integration passed with the independently
+qualified `/var/tmp/foldgpt-bionic-supervisor-8Kd8xQRE` build, running as uid 1000.
+`just test -p codex-exec-server --test native_local_runtime --run-ignored all`
+requires `FOLDGPT_NATIVE_FACTORY_BUILD` explicitly; without the prerequisite it
+cannot silently substitute a fake server. The test verifies exact serialized
+process and filesystem policy, all environment-policy fields, real cwd/env,
+separate stdout/stderr, actual stdin EOF, binary stdin/stdout, exit 23, successful
+file reads/writes, forbidden-path and unsupported-TTY refusals before mutation,
+managed-network refusal, and closure of a live worker's transport. Previously
+cloned execution/filesystem backends both reject later requests. An independent
+observer retains the actual supervisor result and termination status after RPC
+loss; all three workers report native cleanup and the interrupted worker reports
+`cancelled`. No second start or replacement server is observed.
+
+Evidence: `C:/Dev/foldgpt-engine-native-runtime-tests.log`. This test exercises the
+injected environment boundary, not the complete application/model loop on Android.
+The matching library selection passed 27 tests (268 filtered), covering local
+registration including the `ExecutorOnly` refusal, client disconnect/recovery,
+process event ordering, network admission, and previous remote filesystem cwd
+behavior. Evidence: `C:/Dev/foldgpt-engine-native-runtime-regression.log`.
+
+The metadata/shell follow-up passed 41 selected core and exec-server library
+tests, including the six new runtime metadata cases, existing local/remote shell
+selection and the preserved `ExecutorOnly` registration refusal. The active V1
+snapshot test proves the controller does not launch the runtime shell, with an
+ordinary local positive control that actually creates its marker. An injected
+runtime also selects direct execution when the controller uses `ZshFork`.
+
+The selected model-dispatch integration passed with a real PC executable under
+an alternate runtime basename, the explicit reported shell path and `login:true`.
+Although the controller enables V2 snapshots, the runtime reports the capability
